  "idea": "Loom vs Tella: which screen recording tool makes better client demos",
  "text": "Loom is great for quick internal chats, but Tella makes you look like a production studio. Sending prospects a raw Loom link means sharing awkward pauses, unedited stumbles, and desktop clutter. Low presentation quality undermines your brand credibility and hurts high-ticket conversion rates. Tella lets you record multiple takes, crop interfaces dynamically, and apply studio backgrounds without technical editing. This closes more premium clients without extra stress.",
